---
name: plan-hardening-final
version: 1.0.0
description: The closing plan-hardening wisp, created after the last iteration's fix step closes. ceremony-qa reviews the plan after the final critical-plan-reviewer pass, the planner fixes, and one verify pass closes the fixed findings.
format: toml
required_variables:
  - root
  - phase
  - planner
---
{#
Rendered with `sc-compose bead render` to a .formula.toml and created with
`bd mol wisp <file>` only after the last iteration wisp's fix step closes, so
the ceremony step always follows the final critical-plan-reviewer pass.
#}
formula = "plan-hardening-final"
description = "Plan hardening of {{{ root }}}: ceremony review, fixes and verification."
version = 1
type = "workflow"
phase = "vapor"

[[steps]]
id = "ceremony"
title = "{{{ root }}} hardening final: ceremony-qa pass"
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:plan-hardening"]
metadata = { pass = "ceremony", root = "{{{ root }}}", planner = "{{{ planner }}}", iteration = "final" }
description = """
Pass: ceremony-qa. Your review instructions are the agent file
`.claude/agents/ceremony-qa.md`, with the plan beads as its review targets.
It recommends removals only.

The plan is the phase root {{{ root }}} and its sprint containers. Read them
with the plan block of your dispatch template.

1. Review the whole plan as the agent file says and file every finding with
   the finding block. The planner is {{{ planner }}}.
2. Close this step: PASS when you filed no Blocking or Important finding,
   FAIL otherwise.
"""

[[steps]]
id = "fix"
title = "{{{ root }}} hardening final: planner fixes"
needs = ["ceremony"]
assignee = "{{{ planner }}}"
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:plan-hardening"]
metadata = { pass = "fix", root = "{{{ root }}}", planner = "{{{ planner }}}", iteration = "final" }
description = """
Planner {{{ planner }}}: fix the plan for every open fix bead under
{{{ root }}}: the ceremony findings and any critical-plan-reviewer findings
from the last iteration. A FAIL from that final critical pass is normal.

1. `bd list --parent {{{ root }}} -l stage:plan-fix --assignee {{{ planner }}} --status open -n 0 --json`.
2. For each one, change the plan beads with `bd update` and add a
   `fixed: ...` or `rebutted: <citation>` note. Never close a fix bead.
3. Re-run `.claude/skills/atm-beads/scripts/validate-plan --phase {{{ phase }}}`;
   when the plan changed, re-run
   `.claude/skills/sprint-review/scripts/sprint-review --root {{{ root }}}` and
   push the DAG to the plan PR.
4. Close this step when every fix bead has a note.
"""

[[steps]]
id = "verify"
title = "{{{ root }}} hardening final: verify fixes"
needs = ["fix"]
labels = ["phase-{{{ phase }}}", "stage:plan-hardening"]
metadata = { pass = "verify", root = "{{{ root }}}", planner = "{{{ planner }}}", iteration = "final" }
description = """
Pass: verify. For each open `stage:plan-fix` bead under {{{ root }}}, read
the agent file of the pass that filed it (`metadata.pass`: scope is
`.claude/agents/plan-scope-reviewer.md`, critical is
`.claude/agents/critical-plan-reviewer.md`, ceremony is
`.claude/agents/ceremony-qa.md`, lead and adversary findings name their own
check) and check only that finding against the plan.

1. Close each fix bead the plan now resolves. A rebuttal that cites the
   design closes it too. Leave the others open with a note saying what is
   still wrong; file nothing new.
2. Close this step: PASS when no Blocking or Important fix bead is open,
   FAIL otherwise. The open ones go to quality-mgr plan review with the plan.
"""
